# KWarner preview PDF (program report printout)

When the user asks for **PDF creation, PDF updates, printout layout, or program-report print changes**, work in the **KWarner locked preview pipeline** — not the web UI unless they explicitly ask for web.

## Pipeline (source of truth)

| Piece | Path |
|-------|------|
| Renderer | `server/pdf/renderProgramReportKwarnerLockedPreview.js` |
| Shared draw helpers | `server/pdf/drawSeminar.js`, `server/pdf/drawFrame.js` |
| Macro signal data | `js/foodPlanPrintout.js` (`MACRO_SIGNAL_ROWS`, `drawMacroSignalTable`) |
| Payload | `js/programReportPrintout.js` |
| Staples / veg-fruit / flavor kits | `data/cuttingStaplesPrintout.js`, `menuplanner/data/flavorKits.js` |
| Typography tokens | `js/printTemplateTypography.js` |

**Not in scope** unless requested: `program-report/js/report.js` (web shell), production `server/pdf/renderProgramReport.js` (narrative lesson format).

## Mandatory after every PDF change

1. Run **`npm run render:kwarner-preview`** (or `node scripts/render-kwarner-locked-preview.mjs`).
2. The script **always writes a new file** — `docs/samples/kwarner-preview-kristi-veg-fruit-vN.pdf` — by scanning for the highest existing `vN` and incrementing. **Never overwrite** an existing version.
3. It also refreshes stable open paths: `docs/samples/kwarner-preview-kristi-latest.pdf` and `program-report/samples/kwarner-preview-latest.pdf` (use this link in preview mode).
4. Commit the **new versioned PDF**, both **latest** copies, and auto-updated `js/kwarnerPreviewBuild.js`.
5. Tell the user the **new filename** (e.g. `v12`) and **paste a direct download link** in the response:

   - **Latest (always use this):** `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/koryedwards-del/landing-burn-and-build/main/docs/samples/kwarner-preview-kristi-latest.pdf`
   - **Versioned:** `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/koryedwards-del/landing-burn-and-build/main/docs/samples/<PREVIEW_PDF_NAME>`
   - **After Pages deploy:** `https://burnandbuilddiet.com/docs/samples/kwarner-preview-kristi-latest.pdf`

   Do not tell the user to run local commands unless they ask — give them a clickable download URL.

Optional sanity check: `npm run verify:pdf`.

## User prompts

Short prompts are enough — e.g. “update macro table border” or “add row to veg list page”. Apply the change in the renderer/data files above, then **always render a new PDF** without being reminded.

## Sample client

Kristi Warner preview package — see `scripts/render-kwarner-locked-preview.mjs` (`KRISTI_FORM`, `KWARNER_WELCOME_COPY`). Output is currently **7 pages** (Welcome, LBA, History, Food Plan, Servings, veg/fruit staples, flavor kits).
